            <h4 style="color: #002147; border-bottom: 2px solid #004080; padding-bottom: 5px; font-size:20px; font-weight:600;">About Er. Dinesh Kumar </h4>
            <p style="font-size:16px; font-family:Arial; line-height:30px; text-align:justify; line-height:30px;color:black;">
                Er. Dinesh Kumar is currently serving as an Assistant Professor at BRBBA Rajkiya Engineering College, Pratapgarh, with an academic background in Electrical Engineering. He is the I/C of student activity cell and SC/ST cell.
                He is pursuing his Doctor of Philosophy (Ph.D.) from Madan Mohan Malaviya University of Technology (MMMUT), Gorakhpur, with a research focus in the area of Power and Energy System Control. He has completed his M.Tech from Institute of Engineering and Technology (IET) Sitapur road Lucknow, specializing in Electrical Engineering.
                Er. Dinesh Kumar has a keen interest in academic research and has published multiple papers in national and international journals and conferences. His recent research centers on the Power and Energy Control System, contributing to advancements in precision in energy control systems for power applications. He is previously entrusted with key responsibilities as the Ex-Head of the Department of Mechanical Engineering.
            </p>


